WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.833
(upbeat music)

00:00:00.833 --> 00:00:01.800
- When it comes to grilled cheese,

00:00:01.800 --> 00:00:03.310
do you believe less is more,

00:00:03.310 --> 00:00:04.640
or more is more?

00:00:04.640 --> 00:00:05.473
Hi!

00:00:05.473 --> 00:00:06.306
I'm Mimo.

00:00:06.306 --> 00:00:07.880
I'm a Culinary Producer at Tasty.

00:00:07.880 --> 00:00:09.570
Today, I'm going to test recipes

00:00:09.570 --> 00:00:12.730
for a three-, six- and
12-ingredient grilled cheese.

00:00:12.730 --> 00:00:14.570
May the best grilled cheese win.

00:00:14.570 --> 00:00:17.790
First up, we're making our
three-ingredient grilled cheese.

00:00:17.790 --> 00:00:19.120
For the first ingredient,

00:00:19.120 --> 00:00:21.520
we are going to start with bread.

00:00:21.520 --> 00:00:22.930
I decide to go with brioche,

00:00:22.930 --> 00:00:26.040
because it's buttery and fluffy
with a hint of sweetness.

00:00:26.040 --> 00:00:28.450
Our next ingredient is butter.

00:00:28.450 --> 00:00:30.010
Everything is better with butter.

00:00:30.010 --> 00:00:32.370
And since we only can
use three ingredients,

00:00:32.370 --> 00:00:33.790
we want to make them count.

00:00:33.790 --> 00:00:36.920
We are going to generously
butter one side of the bread

00:00:36.920 --> 00:00:39.030
and place it on a hot skill.

00:00:39.030 --> 00:00:41.140
And for our third and final ingredient,

00:00:41.140 --> 00:00:43.900
we are adding sliced American cheese.

00:00:43.900 --> 00:00:46.040
And we have picked American cheese

00:00:46.040 --> 00:00:48.110
because it's such a classic.

00:00:48.110 --> 00:00:51.420
Top the bread with three
slices of American cheese,

00:00:51.420 --> 00:00:54.480
place the other slice of
bread on top, butter side up.

00:00:54.480 --> 00:00:57.020
When the bottom slice of
bread is golden brown,

00:00:57.020 --> 00:01:00.270
flip and continue cooking until
the other side has browned

00:01:00.270 --> 00:01:01.950
and the cheese is fully melted.

00:01:01.950 --> 00:01:02.950
And there we have it,

00:01:02.950 --> 00:01:05.170
our classic three-ingredient
grilled cheese.

00:01:05.170 --> 00:01:07.170
Bread, butter, cheese.

00:01:07.170 --> 00:01:08.890
That really might be all you need.

00:01:08.890 --> 00:01:10.740
I guess we will have to wait and see.

00:01:10.740 --> 00:01:14.040
Next up, we have our
six-ingredient grilled cheese.

00:01:14.040 --> 00:01:17.040
Our first two ingredients are
the same as our last version.

00:01:17.040 --> 00:01:19.850
And those are bread and butter.

00:01:19.850 --> 00:01:20.690
For this version,

00:01:20.690 --> 00:01:21.930
we chose sourdough bread,

00:01:21.930 --> 00:01:24.280
because we are looking
for a bread that's hearty

00:01:24.280 --> 00:01:25.890
with a little bit of a tang.

00:01:25.890 --> 00:01:28.070
After we spread the butter on one side

00:01:28.070 --> 00:01:29.440
of each slice of bread,

00:01:29.440 --> 00:01:32.320
we are going to place
them butter side down.

00:01:32.320 --> 00:01:35.060
And now it's time to
introduce our new ingredients.

00:01:35.060 --> 00:01:37.970
Ingredient number three is grated garlic.

00:01:37.970 --> 00:01:39.710
I mean, think about it.

00:01:39.710 --> 00:01:42.500
This is basically becoming a
garlic bread grilled cheese,

00:01:42.500 --> 00:01:44.420
which sounds like a dream come true.

00:01:44.420 --> 00:01:46.920
Ingredient number four is pesto.

00:01:46.920 --> 00:01:48.550
We tried many different options

00:01:48.550 --> 00:01:50.270
for seasonings and condiments,

00:01:50.270 --> 00:01:53.100
but what we realized is
that pesto is the best way

00:01:53.100 --> 00:01:55.320
to bring the flavor home.

00:01:55.320 --> 00:01:57.370
Now, it's time for cheese.

00:01:57.370 --> 00:02:00.290
We are going to pick two
different types of cheese,

00:02:00.290 --> 00:02:03.050
mozzarella and sharp provolone.

00:02:03.050 --> 00:02:04.540
We're using two types of cheese

00:02:04.540 --> 00:02:06.170
because mozzarella is creamy,

00:02:06.170 --> 00:02:07.210
while sharp provolone

00:02:07.210 --> 00:02:09.540
will give our sandwich a nutty flavor.

00:02:09.540 --> 00:02:11.840
And you're probably
noticing that these steps

00:02:11.840 --> 00:02:14.640
are in a bit of a different
order than last time.

00:02:14.640 --> 00:02:16.390
For the three-ingredient grilled cheese,

00:02:16.390 --> 00:02:19.570
we just built the sandwich
right onto the skillet.

00:02:19.570 --> 00:02:22.380
But because we have more
ingredients this time around,

00:02:22.380 --> 00:02:24.540
we are building our entire sandwich first

00:02:24.540 --> 00:02:27.260
to ensure even cooking throughout.

00:02:27.260 --> 00:02:30.170
After cooking for about
five minutes on each side,

00:02:30.170 --> 00:02:32.740
our sandwich is a beautiful golden brown

00:02:32.740 --> 00:02:35.490
and our cheese is nice melted.

00:02:35.490 --> 00:02:36.640
Time to eat.

00:02:36.640 --> 00:02:39.240
Look at that ooey, gooey goodness.

00:02:39.240 --> 00:02:43.080
Let's get started on the
12-ingredient grilled cheese.

00:02:43.080 --> 00:02:46.160
Our first ingredient
is, of course, butter.

00:02:46.160 --> 00:02:48.350
We're going to melt one
tablespoon of butter

00:02:48.350 --> 00:02:49.800
in a small skillet.

00:02:49.800 --> 00:02:52.570
Then add in a quarter cup
of sliced, yellow onions

00:02:52.570 --> 00:02:53.710
and a pinch of salt.

00:02:53.710 --> 00:02:55.680
Yep, I said onions!

00:02:55.680 --> 00:02:57.860
Make sure to stir your onions often

00:02:57.860 --> 00:03:00.240
until they are soft and
starting to caramelize.

00:03:00.240 --> 00:03:03.720
Caramelizing onions usually
takes up to 40 minutes,

00:03:03.720 --> 00:03:06.500
but since we're using
a very small quantity,

00:03:06.500 --> 00:03:08.880
we're cutting ours back to 10 minutes.

00:03:08.880 --> 00:03:11.890
Next, add in a generous
amount of brown sugar

00:03:11.890 --> 00:03:13.760
and continue cooking the onions

00:03:13.760 --> 00:03:16.040
until the sugar starts to caramelize.

00:03:16.040 --> 00:03:18.365
Add balsamic glaze and stir.

00:03:18.365 --> 00:03:21.160
By cooking these beautiful
caramelized onions,

00:03:21.160 --> 00:03:23.830
we will add in some
sweetness to our final dish.

00:03:23.830 --> 00:03:27.020
Next up, ingredient number six, thyme.

00:03:27.020 --> 00:03:27.853
In a small pot,

00:03:27.853 --> 00:03:29.890
combine the rest of your
butter and the thyme

00:03:29.890 --> 00:03:32.090
to create a delicious infused butter.

00:03:32.090 --> 00:03:35.570
This simple hack is going
to be a game changer.

00:03:35.570 --> 00:03:37.520
We're going to brush our infused butter

00:03:38.444 --> 00:03:41.560
into ingredient number seven, our bread.

00:03:41.560 --> 00:03:42.700
For this recipe,

00:03:42.700 --> 00:03:44.720
we went with artisanal country bread

00:03:44.720 --> 00:03:47.170
with a thick crust and of course, texture.

00:03:47.170 --> 00:03:50.000
This thyme-infused butter
will take our bread

00:03:50.000 --> 00:03:51.300
to the next level.

00:03:51.300 --> 00:03:54.790
That is why we're brushing a
generous amount on both sides.

00:03:54.790 --> 00:03:56.810
Now, it's time to fry.

00:03:56.810 --> 00:03:59.410
Everyone has their own
grilled cheese preference,

00:03:59.410 --> 00:04:01.040
but I think we can all agree

00:04:01.040 --> 00:04:04.660
that we want the bread to
be golden brown and crispy.

00:04:04.660 --> 00:04:07.150
Now, we are going to start assembly.

00:04:07.150 --> 00:04:09.440
This is definitely way more work

00:04:09.440 --> 00:04:11.010
than the average grilled cheese,

00:04:11.010 --> 00:04:12.110
but trust us,

00:04:12.110 --> 00:04:14.340
the outcome will totally be worth it.

00:04:14.340 --> 00:04:15.740
Ingredient number eight.

00:04:15.740 --> 00:04:17.860
Coarse-ground Dijon mustard.

00:04:17.860 --> 00:04:21.070
Spread the mustard evenly
on both slices of bread.

00:04:21.070 --> 00:04:23.070
Next up, aged cheddar.

00:04:23.070 --> 00:04:25.023
We're going to add the shredded cheese.

00:04:25.861 --> 00:04:26.694
Next, ham.

00:04:26.694 --> 00:04:29.040
This is not just a ham
and cheese sandwich.

00:04:29.040 --> 00:04:31.550
This is an upgraded grilled cheese.

00:04:31.550 --> 00:04:33.820
Our next cheese is Gruyere.

00:04:33.820 --> 00:04:37.000
Gruyere is rich, creamy and salty,

00:04:37.000 --> 00:04:39.430
while the aged cheddar is sharp.

00:04:39.430 --> 00:04:41.350
On our other slice of bread,

00:04:41.350 --> 00:04:43.120
add the caramelized onions.

00:04:43.120 --> 00:04:44.240
Sandwich it up!

00:04:44.240 --> 00:04:46.290
Before we throw this back on the heat,

00:04:46.290 --> 00:04:50.070
let's sprinkle the pan with
our 12th and final ingredient,

00:04:50.070 --> 00:04:51.233
Parmesan cheese.

00:04:51.233 --> 00:04:55.140
We will then carefully
place our sandwich on top

00:04:55.140 --> 00:04:56.750
of the Parmesan cheese.

00:04:56.750 --> 00:04:59.250
While the Parmesan cheese
melts and crisps up

00:04:59.250 --> 00:05:00.480
to create a crust,

00:05:00.480 --> 00:05:02.823
we're going to top the
other side of our sandwich

00:05:02.823 --> 00:05:04.920
with the rest of the Parmesan.

00:05:04.920 --> 00:05:08.380
This is my favorite hack to
get our bread nice and crispy,

00:05:08.380 --> 00:05:11.560
which will really make a
difference in the final sandwich.

00:05:11.560 --> 00:05:15.030
Since both slices of bread
are a beautiful color

00:05:15.030 --> 00:05:16.620
and our cheese is melted,

00:05:16.620 --> 00:05:17.940
it's time to plate.

00:05:17.940 --> 00:05:19.180
Here we have it.

00:05:19.180 --> 00:05:21.540
Our 12-ingredient grilled cheese.

00:05:21.540 --> 00:05:24.500
Not only do we have a
creamy, cheesy interior,

00:05:24.500 --> 00:05:27.150
but we have a crispy Parmesan crust,

00:05:27.150 --> 00:05:30.620
sweet caramelized onions
and a kick from the mustard.

00:05:30.620 --> 00:05:32.210
And there we have it.

00:05:32.210 --> 00:05:33.630
Our three-ingredient,

00:05:33.630 --> 00:05:37.400
six-ingredient and
12-ingredient grilled cheese.

00:05:37.400 --> 00:05:40.200
When picking my favorite
sandwich between the three,

00:05:40.200 --> 00:05:42.140
I had to consider flavor,

00:05:42.140 --> 00:05:45.370
texture and which sandwich
I would want to eat again.

00:05:45.370 --> 00:05:47.260
I love how easy and classic

00:05:47.260 --> 00:05:49.220
the three-ingredient grilled cheese is.

00:05:49.220 --> 00:05:51.130
And the pesto and cheese combo

00:05:51.130 --> 00:05:54.800
in the six-ingredient grilled
cheese tasted so great.

00:05:54.800 --> 00:05:56.950
But, at the end of the day,

00:05:56.950 --> 00:05:59.140
I keep going back for more bites

00:05:59.140 --> 00:06:01.440
of the 12-ingredient grilled cheese.

00:06:01.440 --> 00:06:02.650
Thanks for joining me

00:06:02.650 --> 00:06:06.620
as I test our favorite three
grilled cheese sandwiches.

00:06:06.620 --> 00:06:07.960
Let us know how you make

00:06:07.960 --> 00:06:09.860
your favorite grilled cheese at home.

00:06:09.860 --> 00:06:10.761
Bye!

00:06:10.761 --> 00:06:13.594
(energetic music)

